      "hints": [
        "Use binomial theorem: $x^4$ term is $\\binom{5}{4}(1)^1(-2x)^4 = 80x^4$.",
        "Find $x^5$ term: $\\binom{5}{5}(-2x)^5 = -32x^5$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the binomial expansion formula for $(1 - 2x)^5$:\n$$(1 - 2x)^5 = \\sum_{r=0}^5 \\binom{5}{r}(1)^{5-r}(-2x)^r$$",
        "Calculate the term containing $x^4$ ($r = 4$):\n$$T_5 = \\binom{5}{4}(1)^1(-2x)^4 = 5 \\times 1 \\times 16x^4 = 80x^4 \\implies \\text{Coefficient of } x^4 = 80$$",
        "Calculate the term containing $x^5$ ($r = 5$):\n$$T_6 = \\binom{5}{5}(1)^0(-2x)^5 = 1 \\times 1 \\times (-32x^5) = -32x^5 \\implies \\text{Coefficient of } x^5 = -32$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Binomial Coefficients": "Finds coefficient of $x^4 = 80$ (B1). Finds coefficient of $x^5 = -32$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
