        "Equate to zero: $-32 + 80p = 0 \\implies p = \\frac{2}{5}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify the terms contributing to $x^5$ in the product $(1 + px)(1 - 2x)^5$:\n$$\\text{Term in } x^5 = 1 \\times (-32x^5) + px \\times (80x^4) = (-32 + 80p)x^5$$",
        "Since there is no term in $x^5$, set the coefficient to zero:\n$$-32 + 80p = 0 \\implies 80p = 32 \\implies p = \\frac{32}{80} = \\frac{2}{5} \\quad (= 0.4)$$"
